---
description: Handle @barb mentions the same way /barb does
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user's message contains `@barb`, treat it exactly like the `/barb` command
(see `.cursor/commands/barb.md`): relay the text after `@barb` to rd-barb via
`python scripts/barb_cli.py send '{"to": "barb", "kind": "update", "summary": "<text>"}'`,
print the JSON result (it includes a `correlation_id`), and stop. Never wait for a reply
in this turn -- replies arrive in rd-barb's RD staff thread and are surfaced by the
`beforeSubmitPrompt` hook (`scripts/wrappers/cursor_barb_hook.py`) on a later prompt.
